## ✓ Bug Fixed

**Issue:** Session expiration boundary condition — sessions were still valid at the exact millisecond they expired.

**Root Cause:** In `/src/auth/session.js:3`, the `isExpired()` function used `now > expiresAt` instead of `now >= expiresAt`. This allowed sessions to remain valid when `now === expiresAt`.

**Fix Applied:** Changed the comparison operator from `>` to `>=`

```javascript
// Before
return now > expiresAt;

// After
return now >= expiresAt;
```

Now sessions are correctly invalid the instant they reach their expiration time, matching the documented behavior: "At the expiry instant it is over." This fix applies throughout the codebase since all expiration checks (middleware, refresh API, cleanup jobs) use this single `isExpired()` function.
